# REQ-003: Scanning & Document Upload

**Priority:** Must Have (upload + preview)
**Phase:** Documents Management Core (30-day delivery)
**Effort:** Low
**Risk:** Medium
**Depends On:** REQ-001 (Unified Inbound Document Inbox)

---

## User Story

As a practice administrator,
I need to scan paper documents and upload files into the document management system with a preview step before committing,
So that I can verify documents are complete and legible before they enter the inbox workflow.

**Acceptance Criteria:**
- [ ] Users can upload one or more documents from disk (any supported file format — see REQ-005) into the inbox. Multiple files may be selected in a single file-picker interaction. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Users can drag one or more files from the local file system and drop them onto the upload dialog to initiate an upload. Dropped files proceed through the same sequential individual preview workflow as file-picker uploads. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Before any document is committed to the inbox, the user is presented with a preview of that document using the same document viewer component used in the main workflow, rendering the actual uploaded document content. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] When multiple files are selected, each file is previewed and confirmed or discarded individually and in sequence. Users cannot bulk-commit all selected files in a single action without reviewing each file’s preview. *(Must Have — clinical safety)*
- [ ] If a user discards one file during a multi-file upload sequence, the remaining files in the batch continue through the preview sequence unaffected. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The user can confirm or discard each document from the preview step before it is submitted. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Upload entry points are clearly accessible from the inbox without navigating away. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] During the preview step, the user can manually enter or edit filing metadata for the document (document type, date of care, date received, document title) before confirming. Metadata entered during upload is carried forward as pre-populated values in the Filing Queue. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] For a single-document upload, preview and filing actions are completed in one continuous flow before submission. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] For a multiple-document upload, confirmed documents are routed to the Unmatched list for review and processing. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] Documents uploaded manually are assigned source status **Manual Upload** in triage metadata. *(Must Have)*
- [ ] The upload experience must not show a user-facing banner for direct scanner TWAIN availability in this release. *(Must Have)*

> **Out of scope for Documents Management Core:** Direct scanner integration via TWAIN driver is not included in this release. Deferred to Phase 2 pending driver procurement resolution. Upload from disk is the only supported ingest path in Core, and no user-facing TWAIN availability banner is shown.

