### Accessibility Requirements (WCAG 2.1 AA)

**Checklist:**
- [x] Perceivable: drag-zone has `role="region"` + `aria-label`; file type list is text not icon-only; error state uses `role="alert"`
- [x] Operable: full keyboard path via Browse button (no drag required); all actions Tab-navigable; Confirm disabled state communicated via `aria-disabled`
- [x] Understandable: every form input has `aria-label`; inline error on document type when attempted without selection; CLIN-007 warning visible before any action
- [x] Robust: `jest-axe ^9.0.0`; no native `<button>` or `<input>` outside `@emisgroup/ui-*` except hidden file input (browser-native, accessibility-neutral)

**Rule A — all inputs labelled:**
```tsx
<Select aria-label={t('upload.meta.docType')} ... />
<DatePicker aria-label={t('upload.meta.dateOfCare')} ... />
<Input aria-label={t('upload.meta.title')} clearable ... />
```

**Rule B — loading and error states announced:**
```tsx
// Batch progress
<div role="status" aria-live="polite">{t('upload.batch.progress', { current, total })}</div>
// Invalid file
<div role="alert" aria-live="assertive">{t('upload.error.rejected.heading')}</div>
```

**Rule C — automated testing:**
```tsx
it('upload zone has no accessibility violations', async () => {
  const { container } = render(<UploadZone />);
  expect(await axe(container)).toHaveNoViolations();
});
```

